  "summary": "Group commit of the SQLite store for one caller (SqliteStore::apply_group in group.rs, record 0045; delivered by group_responses_into in writer.rs on the single reply lane of the default single-owner runtime): the members of a group run in one transaction with a savepoint each, a refused member is undone alone, the answers leave only after the one COMMIT, a kill before it loses the whole group with no answer handed over, a commit that failed makes every member unknown, and so does a commit that is durable and whose call returns an error; the caller then reconciles each member by its identity, which never gives an operation a second effect. Outside the model: the groups of the log and volatile stores (LogStore::apply_group, VolatileStore::apply_group), and with --delivery-shards K >= 1 the formation of a group from 1 + K owner lanes and the delivery of its answers to several owners.",
