sts/writer_group_kill.rs", "test": "a_worker_killed_after_one_answer_of_its_group_left_every_member"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/tests/writer_group_kill.rs", "test": "a_worker_killed_after_two_answers_of_its_group_left_every_member"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/tests/writer_group_kill.rs", "test": "a_worker_killed_after_three_answers_of_its_group_left_every_member"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/tests/writer_group_kill.rs", "test": "a_worker_killed_after_all_answers_but_one_of_its_group_left_every_member"}],
  "not_replayed": "No test replays a mutant that releases an answer early (mut-release-before-commit, mut-release-at-savepoint): apply_group returns its answers only after the commit, so the defect cannot be driven without changing the function. No test replays mut-uncertain-is-not-committed: the store recognises an operation by its receipt whatever the caller believes, so a second effect cannot be driven without removing the recognition reads; the replays show the recognition instead. No test fences a member after a commit that failed through the product worker (reach-fence-after-failure is replayed on the store alone, by a_group_on_a_failing_medium_leaves_nothing_and_says_nothing_certain). No test makes the meta row of a group fail to be written, and none delivers the answers of one group to several owners. The tests of commit_error_tests.rs run in a build with the feature kill-points.",
